the duchess of sussex has won her high  court privacy claim against the mail on  sunday over the publication of a  personal and private  handwritten letter to her estranged  father meghan markle said in a statement  that she was grateful that associated  newspapers  and the mail on sunday had been held to  account  sky's royal correspondent rihanna mills  joins me now so  rihanna on the face of it a big win this  for meghan markle  this will be seen as a huge victory by  the sussexes this evening who  over recent years have made it very  clear that they would  hold those to account that they felt  over the years have  victimized them have run untrue stories  about them and this evening we found out  that mr justice warby who is the judge  who's been overseeing this case between  megan  and associated newspapers has ruled in  her favor and allowed the fact that this  will not  go to trial he has decided that she has  won  her case now if i read out her statement  to you i think it shows just how  pleased they are with that verdict this  evening the duchess of sussex has said  after two long years of pursuing  litigation i'm grateful to the courts  for holding associated newspapers and  the mail on sunday to account  for their illegal and dehumanizing  practices  these tactics and those of their sister  publications mail online and the daily  mail  are not new in fact they've been going  on for far too long  without consequence for these outlets  it's a game  for me and so many others it's real life  real relationships and very real sadness  the damage they've done and continue to  do runs deep  she goes on to say i share this victory  with each of you  because we all deserve justice and truth  and we all  deserve better now just to remind  everyone this case  revolved around a letter that was  published by the mail on sunday in  february  2019 a letter that megan had written to  her father  talking about the upset that he'd caused  by sharing  personal details about their  relationship by talking to various  newspapers now  megan's father all along said that he  went to the newspaper with that letter  because megan's friends had previously  talked about that letter  in an interview that they had done with  people magazine  however mr justice warby today has said  the claimant still had  a reasonable expectation that the  contents of that letter  would uh remain private he said the only  terrible justification for any such  interference  was to correct some inaccuracies about  the letter but he says for the most part  they did not serve that purpose at all  taken as a whole the disclosures were  manifestly excessive  and hence unlawful now the managing  editor of the mail on sunday robin kelly  has responded this evening  by saying that we're very surprised by  today's summary judgment  and disappointed of being denied the  chance to have all the evidence  heard and tested in open court at a full  trial  they say we're carefully considering the  judgement contents  and will decide in due course whether to  lodge  an appeal now it is worth pointing out  the judge said there is one  element to this case that should  potentially still go to trial  and that is around copyright who exactly  owns the copyright because there is a  suggestion  that actually megan was helped by some  palace staff when it came to writing  that letter but certainly i think  the sussexes will be breathing a sigh of  relief they wanted to avoid  a huge show trial where you would have  father and daughter giving evidence  against each other and that is something  that they have managed to avoid  and i think also sending a clear message  to the tabloids that they will not  put up with stories that they say are  inaccurate and false  yeah and just briefly rhiannon the  background is the couple's  difficult very difficult relationship  with the press  oh yeah i will never forget the end of  that tour in south africa where it was  announced that megan was going to take  this  legal action against the mail on sunday  and the accompanying statement that we  had from prince harry  a 10-paragraph statement in which he  alluded to  the fact that he believes that stories  that were written about his mother the  way that the tabloids and the paparazzi  pursued her eventually led to her death  in some way and the fact that he said  that he was not going to allow that to  happen  to another woman in his life he of  course has been fiercely protective  of megan and also his son archie only  last week we also saw him  uh prince harry win uh his court battle  against  again the mail on sunday uh for claiming  that he had not been in contact  with the royal marines of course this is  completely different from what we'd  usually expect from mems the royal  family who have that mantra  of never complain never explained but  certainly the sussexes are very  different they are definitely  convinced that they will take things to  court if they think that they have  a case to pursue and this evening they  will be  feeling some sense of relief that in  some ways this brings to  to an end what they call two years a  very difficult litigation  um but yeah they are not afraid to take  on those who they feel  and not writing the correct things about  them and  are intruding into their privacy too  much
 

